WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.975
Here's the uncomfortable fact: disabling
an account doesn't revoke a certificate.

2
00:00:04.975 --> 00:00:09.452
The PIV card is bound to the Entra
user through an attribute holding the

3
00:00:09.452 --> 00:00:12.107
certificate's identifiers, and the strong,

4
00:00:12.107 --> 00:00:15.825
high-affinity bindings identify
exactly one certificate.

5
00:00:15.825 --> 00:00:20.950
So every reissue or renewal means the
card system has to rewrite the binding.

6
00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:23.650
Who can write it depends on
where the user is mastered.

7
00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:28.588
Today, for synced users, only Entra
Connect can, from Active Directory.

8
00:00:28.588 --> 00:00:31.987
Once the account moves to the
cloud, the design guidance is

9
00:00:31.987 --> 00:00:35.600
that the card system's issuance
event writes it through Graph.

10
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:40.050
And the warning in red: whoever writes
that value decides who signs in.

11
00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:41.640
Next, revocation.
